From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:08:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Wire up the PMIC
 interrupt

The IRQ pin of the AXP318W is the net PMU-IRQ. It has a pull-up and
goes to the NMI pad of the SoC as AP-NMI, so it is active low.

Describe it, so that the PMIC events reach Linux.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards, both quiet at rest; on
one of them a short of the power key test pads raised the PMIC
interrupt once per edge.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index c420665654c5..6acd4c657b37 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -316,6 +316,7 @@ &r_i2c0 {
 	axp318: pmic@36 {
 		compatible = "x-powers,axp318w";
 		reg = <0x36>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&nmi_intc 0 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 		interrupt-controller;
 		#interrupt-cells = <1>;
 
